{
  // Extends the shared base rather than restating its flags — a hand-copied
  // strict-flag set drifts silently: `strict` does not imply `noUnusedLocals`,
  // `noImplicitReturns` or `noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature`, so a pin file
  // could pass here while the real build rejects it, which defeats the point of
  // a project whose whole job is to catch what the other passes miss.
  //
  // It used to extend `packages/jssdk/tsconfig.json` — the package *build*
  // config — so a build-motivated edit there reached into this gate with no
  // signal to whoever made it. #396 inverted that: both now extend the same
  // base, and this file needs no `rootDir` override, because the base does not
  // emit declarations and so infers no `rootDir` to be outside of.
  //
  // Scope: **every** `.ts` under `test/`, not only the `*.types.spec.ts` pins.
  // It used to be the pins alone, and that left the rest of the tree compiled
  // by nobody — esbuild strips types without checking them. A spec could assert
  // against a shape the SDK does not have and only a live-portal run would ever
  // notice; #425 is the case that made this worth fixing, where six cases read
  // `getData()!.result` off a `Result<T[]>` and `.result` on an array is not a
  // type error anyone was looking for (#428).
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // Relaxed for tests only, and deliberately. The flag forbids `obj.foo` when
    // `foo` comes from an index signature, which is right for library source
    // and wrong here: a test reaching into a portal payload or a batch result
    // keyed by command name does exactly that, on purpose, ~218 times. Turning
    // it on would trade real type coverage for a bracket-notation rewrite that
    // makes the assertions harder to read.
    "noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature": false,
    "types": ["node", "vitest/globals"]
  },
  "include": ["./**/*.ts"],
  //
  // Note what this drags in: `test/integration/skills-recipes/*.spec.ts` imports
  // the recipe files under `skills/b24jssdk-recipes/`, so those — and their
  // `grammy` / `node-cron` / `openai` dependencies — are part of this program.
  // Those deps live in a non-workspace package that the root `pnpm install`
  // does not touch, which is why `test:typecheck` and `package-jssdk:test:run-types`
  // both run `skills:install` first. Without it the pass fails on a module it
  // was never asked about, in a workspace the diff did not touch (#428).
  // The two `test/integration/docs/**` specs import the docs Nuxt app, whose
  // modules rely on Nuxt's auto-imports and generated types. Those resolve
  // under `docs:typecheck` and cannot resolve here, so the docs app is checked
  // by its own pass and these two specs sit outside this one. Excluding a spec
  // is a real gap, not a tidy-up — if a third one appears, widen the pass
  // rather than the exclusion.
  "exclude": [
    "../node_modules",
    "./integration/docs/**"
  ]
}
